WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.760
This is the proposed budget
for the new project.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.810
It's 148.5 billion yen?

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.480
Give us a break.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:15.020
Presenting this to the National Diet
without disclosing the contents is absurd.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.980
Then does the future
of our country not matter?

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.400
Regardless, we would need the
Imperial Household Agency to share duties.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.280
Iboshi.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.950
If you're going to go this far,
failure is not an option.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.040
Please leave it to me.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.670
In the end, love will win.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.200
The flight test program
is being postponed a quarter!

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.820
Ah, jeez!
It's those damn Dragon Pilots' fault!

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.450
Why us?

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:36.080
Well, the choice comes down to
the close proximity of the bedrooms.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.620
Even so,

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:40.710
I didn't sign up for
the Self-Defense Force to do this.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.750
-I feel the same.
-Huh?

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:45.170
But we cannot refuse orders from the top.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.090
That's what it means to be public servants
so it can't be helped, can it?

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:50.050
What's up with her?

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.600
Even Flight Leader Kakiyasu questions it.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.310
Pardon me.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.350
The order from the top
is a bit too much this time.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.230
Huh? What kind of order?

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:02.940
Love.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:04.900
Love?

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:09.570
You did very well, Masotan.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:12.910
Living on a deserted island
must've been tough.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.660
Okonogi, you were lonely, weren't you?

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:16.990
Yeah, I guess so.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.210
When Masotan was gone, I...

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:22.040
No, no. I'm talking about Amakasu.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:23.130
Huh?

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.420
It's quite amazing, Okonogi,

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.260
that you can actually treat
Amakasu like a woman.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.470
Your strike zone is too big.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.010
W-What are you talking about?

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.680
Hey, Masotan!

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.770
Were you waiting for me?

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.350
Or not? Which is it?

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:42.560
Amakasu!

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.230
Oh, Okonogi, too.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.230
Were you waiting for me?

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:47.940
Just kidding.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.360
There's no way I'd be waiting for you!

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:54.950
You don't need to deny it so strongly.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.330
I was just joking.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:59.250
Ah, I'm sorry! That's not what I meant...

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:00.410
Oh, by the way,

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:04.420
Flight Leader Kakiyasu was waiting--
No, I mean, searching.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.920
For you.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.250
Huh?

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.590
Vice-Minister Iboshi has given us
quite the challenge.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.510
The White Lovers.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.890
Lacking confidence in themselves,

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:21.180
the girls harbor an obscure blank space
in their hearts.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:25.310
It's only when those girls
coexist with the OTF

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.440
that they realize their own worth.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.190
Only the OTF is in their hearts.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.860
When they are
in a dependent state of mind,

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:36.990
they are able to truly connect
with the OTF.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:41.660
However, the Dragon Pilots until now
have failed completely.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:42.620
For the most part.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:44.540
A love affair, huh?

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.460
Precisely.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:48.960
Love is what blinds young girls

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.380
so they no longer depend on the OTF.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:56.220
Drastic measures
are necessary to prevent that.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:58.180
Eliminate love.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.310
And purify the love
they have for their OTF.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:02.680
Yes.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.140
The White Lovers...

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.310
will be painted black.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.070
Make the Dragon Pilots fall in love once

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.780
then crush it thoroughly into dust.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:14.650
W-What does that mean?

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:20.080
If they're hit with a traumatizing blow,
they'll never speak of love again.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.540
Supposedly.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:23.870
But even then, that is--

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.750
Thank you for waiting!

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.040
Uh... Um...

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:32.800
This is Sergeant Akishima
of the 2nd Air Depot, General Affairs.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:36.760
Recently, romance within the base in Gifu
seems to be on the decline.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:40.390
When Self-Defense Force members marry
one another, the turnover rate drops.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:43.930
Sergeant Akishima is to investigate
the base for information on love.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:45.270
That is all.

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:48.150
Huh? But didn't you just say differently?

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:49.150
Understood.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.070
The Sotoori Strategy, right?

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.780
Sotoori Strategy?

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:57.320
Leave it to me,
Gifu's number one love expert!

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:03.620
First, the one with the most
promising prospects is El Hoshino.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:07.870
Captain Zaito, the bad boy of Gifu,
already has eyes on her.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:09.920
Next, we have Mayumi Hitomi.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.800
Maternal types are quite popular
in the Air Self-Defense Force.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.130
What about Amakasu?

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:19.590
Amakasu's one and only choice
is right here.

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:20.850
M-Me?

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.560
Rather, there are no other dark horses
or rivals in the running.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:25.930
Wait a minute!

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.310
Like I said before,

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:30.060
I don't have any feelings towards Amakasu!

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:30.980
Before?

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.060
Uh...

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:33.480
Sergeant Akishima,

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:37.280
I expect your execution of
the Sotoori Strategy will go well.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:38.450
Yes, Sir!

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:42.990
Airman 1st Class Okonogi's
show of resistance is natural.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:47.250
However, I can understand
Vice-Minister Iboshi's fears.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.370
There was that incident with Forest.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.250
I know it well.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:55.000
After Moriyama fell in love, she wasn't on
the same wavelength as her OTF.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:56.630
And once she got pregnant.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:00.640
If only you could have
locked down Tamaru...

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:09.310
Come to think of it, there was no one
chosen for Kinutsugai.

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:11.850
They're out of Weekly Young Jump.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:15.730
No Young Jump.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.360
I can't read this week's "Kingdom."
Huh?

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:26.740
"Kingdom!"

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.700
T-This is...

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.580
undoubtedly this week's chapter.

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:34.710
But why is it here?

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:53.230
This is blatantly suspicious,
but I can't stop.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:05.240
Do you want to read what happens next?

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:12.080
Throughout history in all places,
when a number of women gather,

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:15.210
the ensuing girl talk
will lead to the topic of love.

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:17.460
Or so I'm told.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:23.470
I want you to pass on to me the contents
of your girls talk with the Dragon Pilots.

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:24.470
Why?

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:26.470
I wonder why indeed.

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:30.980
Nevermind. I'm not that curious about it.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:32.020
That's true.

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:35.270
There is nothing more interesting
to you than "Kingdom."

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:39.150
It's possible that
you will never fall victim to love.

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:40.070
Huh?

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:43.900
This is a list of all the things I want
to know from the girls talk.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:48.410
For each topic answered, I will reward you
with one page of "Kingdom."

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:51.870
Why is it asking
about favorite confections?

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.660
I wonder why indeed.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:56.250
I don't need to know.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:59.670
More importantly, "Kingdom" is typically
18 pages per week.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.550
I've already read 16 pages, which means
there's only two pages left.

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:07.720
Actually...

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.560
I have the continuation right here.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.480
H-How?

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:15.440
If you want to read the rest...

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:17.560
you know what to do, right?

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:22.320
It's rare for you
to invite us out, Lilikos!

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:23.940
Yeah. Sure.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.360
Even Hoshino came.
Isn't it great, Hitomin?

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:28.410
Yes, it is.

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:30.620
What kind of lame name is that?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:34.120
We should give Hoshino
a name too, right, Nao?

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:37.460
-Don't get casual with me!
-Here's the Shishamo smelt!

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:40.000
Yum, Shishamo with smelt eggs!

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.800
These are full of eggs, too!

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:46.430
Back home, we only eat ones
without the eggs.

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:50.350
Ladies, which type do you like?

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:53.020
Oh, I prefer the smelt with eggs.

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.020
No, which male type?

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:58.150
I think male Shishamo are pretty rare, no?

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.820
No, which human male type?

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:03.280
-Huh?
-Why are you asking suddenly?

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.280
It's a little weird for him to have eggs.

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:08.740
Hitomin, we're not talking
about Shishamo anymore.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:14.700
I think I'd like someone
who cherished Futomomo.

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:18.500
-Well, Mr. Ikushima is surely my--
-Oh, I don't need to hear from you.

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:19.710
What?

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:23.300
-What about you, Hisone?
-What a minute...

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.220
I've never thought about it.
What about you, Hoshino?

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:29.050
In any case,

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:31.470
I hate gaudy, tactless men.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.970
I'm asking about the types you like.

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:35.770
I don't like men with crew cuts,

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:39.190
overly friendly men who call me "sweetie,"
men who tell dirty jokes...

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:43.070
I feel like there's a certain person
who fits those traits...

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:46.360
Oh, El, sweetie!
What're you all chatting about?

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:49.280
Let us join you for a drink!

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.280
Waiter! I'll take a beer!

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:52.530
-That's him.
-Medium draft!

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:53.870
Zaito...

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:57.120
-We were having a guy's night...
-Need a refill? Whatcha drinking?

00:10:57.370 --> 00:10:58.580
Calpis sour.

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:01.290
Wow. That's like drinking juice.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:03.380
How adorable!

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:08.420
El!

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:10.430
DOES EL HOSHINO HAVE AFFECTION
FOR CAPTAIN ZAITO?

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:13.430
Not in the least.

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:16.020
Zaito, your beer is here! Medium draft!

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:16.930
Shut up!

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:21.480
<i>Hiso Maso!</i>

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:26.570
<i>The important thing here</i>

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:29.740
<i>is not making</i>
<i>the Dragon Pilots fall in love.</i>

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:33.910
It is to have them fall in love
and then break their hearts.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:35.950
I can't do that!

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.500
Besides, Amakasu doesn't
have feelings for me...

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:42.250
This is for the sake of the new project,

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.080
Airman First Class Okonogi.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:48.010
It is your obligation as a member
of the Okonogi family.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.300
There are two tickets in there.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:54.090
You've been approved to leave the base,
you may freely go.

00:11:57.060 --> 00:11:59.520
An obligation by birth, huh!

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:02.480
Ah! I found you, Okonogi!

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:04.900
A-Amakasu?

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:09.360
I saw you were enjoying a smoke
during your smoking time!

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:11.820
You're drunk, aren't you?

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:13.610
Do you like drinking?

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.240
Nope. I don't get the taste of it...

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:21.910
but since the Dragon Pilots arrived,
I've had more chances to drink.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:24.790
I remember!

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:28.090
I hate you, Okonogi!

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:32.840
I hate and despise you!
You said you'd never wait for me!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:34.010
From this afternoon?

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.180
I hate you.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:37.600
Make it up to me somehow.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.770
Oh... Um...

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:40.930
Here.

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:42.230
Movie?

00:12:42.730 --> 00:12:46.610
Since tomorrow's a holiday,
would you want to go with me?

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:48.940
But, we need permission to leave.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:51.110
Oh, about that, um...

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:55.410
these tickets give you preferential
treatment so you're excused already.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:59.080
That's so convenient!

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:01.080
'Cause it doesn't exist.

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:03.080
Thank you so much!

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.750
I don't hate you, Okonogi!

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.960
Thank you very much.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:19.260
Snooze, snooze...

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:43.330
I just witnessed something major.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:48.460
I haven't filled in a thing.

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:52.840
But how does he have
next week's "Kingdom" already?

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:56.180
He must have some amazing connections.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.220
And who is he in the first place?

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:00.970
It's packed today.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:02.430
May I sit here?

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:03.520
Sure.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:06.730
While you're here, I want to ask you
some questions, Hitomin.

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:12.070
Oh, Onaga! There's a seat over here!

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.780
O-Okay.

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:17.150
Are you alone today?

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:20.160
Yeah. Zaito's got a hangover.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:23.660
He was drowning his sorrows
quite a bit with alcohol last night.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:27.790
Well... he's not a bad guy really.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:32.540
Just sometimes he can be a handful
when he's in front of a girl.

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:35.420
Would you like to eat this, too?

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:37.800
Oh? You don't want it?

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:39.300
Thanks.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:41.600
-Excite, excite.
-Mm...

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:44.720
Take this too, if you want.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:46.770
Okay. Thanks.

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.810
You eat very well,

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:51.400
just like Futomomo!

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:55.070
Can I pet you a little?

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:58.860
Oh, it's hard.

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:01.700
I-I'm... all finished!

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:06.580
It'd be wonderful to see him
get more excited.

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:09.330
You came onto him
like a hostess at a club.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:14.170
Oh no, was I acting
like a pervy old sex offender?

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:17.210
What should I do? I'm remorseful.

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:19.300
You think you're the club's customer?

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:33.020
<i>T-This is ridiculous.</i>

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:35.150
<i>Watching this on a date</i>

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:37.320
<i>hardly makes me look favorable.</i>

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:47.540
Okonogi, everything's delicious.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:51.960
Amakasu, could you put that away
while we eat?

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:53.170
Okay.

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:55.960
That movie was so crappy
that it was refreshing.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:58.760
Huh? But you were crying--

00:15:58.840 --> 00:15:59.670
I'm so sorry!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:03.090
The agony in the zombies's cries
was great background music,

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:04.640
and it made me think.

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:06.220
Think about what?

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:10.140
This was my first time coming
to the movies with a friend.

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:12.770
When you say friend, do you mean me?

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:16.480
S-Sorry!
Was it too much for me to call you that?

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:18.730
N-No, it's an honor.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.280
Same with a flower dance.

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:26.280
I've never experienced hanging out
with friends before.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:31.790
When we were training on the island,
it was fun because it was like camping.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:36.500
That alone was enough
to make every day shine.

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.840
It was so strange. I just started crying.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:42.170
Amakasu, you're amazing, too.

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:43.260
Huh?

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:48.010
My future had always been decided for me,
taking after my parents' work.

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:53.270
Okonogi, your parents were airmen, too?

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:55.850
The tracks were already laid out for me...

00:16:56.100 --> 00:16:59.980
so, I've never thought of
what I truly wanted to do.

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:04.030
The fact that you've fretted over it
and finally found that is--

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:08.030
Okonogi! That is so awesome!

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:09.990
Huh? That's kind,

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:13.120
but all I do is what others tell me to do.

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:16.500
You really like Masotan, right?

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.840
Uh, yeah. I do.

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:23.130
The things you like and the things decided
for you are in agreement.

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:28.600
You've taken your assigned duties
and mixed it with your own will,

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:30.760
and you, Mr. Something Okonogi...

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:34.520
-Um, what's your first name?
-It's Haruto.

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:36.650
And you, Mr. Haruto Okonogi,
burst on the scene!

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:45.530
Okonogi, are you trying out
a new wild look?

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:47.160
No.

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:51.700
I wanted to go shopping after this.
Do you want to go, too?

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:58.880
Sure, I'd be happy to go with you.

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:05.470
At this rate, I'll only
get to read six pages.

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:11.430
Oh?

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:22.770
Hey.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:24.280
What now?

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:27.650
Just wanted to get
the liquor out of my system.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:28.910
I don't care.

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:43.000
I guess there's no spark after all.

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:51.470
How sad!

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:53.760
You actually went all out against a girl.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:56.770
God damn it!

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:58.940
You're too damn cool, El!

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:02.650
Dammit. I'm not going to lose.

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:06.230
I'm... cool?

00:19:12.530 --> 00:19:14.280
Hisone's on a date?

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.200
What a predicament.

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:21.080
Mr. Ikushima, are you interested...

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:23.380
in Amakasu?

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:28.720
Feelings of love will cause over-secretion
of hormones in her body

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:31.550
and distort her suit size!

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:37.020
Masotan! I'm home!

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:44.820
I brought you a souvenir.

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:49.110
I'm sorry, but secondhand flip phones
are surprisingly expensive.

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:52.320
With my salary, I could only
afford to buy five.

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:58.200
These are tokens
of my appreciation for you, Masotan.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:01.460
Because of you, I've made friends.

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.210
Lots of things have happened,

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:05.460
so I'm enjoying every day.

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:07.840
Thank you, Masotan.

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:18.520
T-They noticed?

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:21.640
I'm sorry, Masotan! I'll buy more
next time, but share now--

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:24.150
A... Amakasu?

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:26.650
Futomomo!

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:29.650
-Calm down!
-Go home, Norma!

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:33.240
Even Akemi is getting riled up.

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:35.490
Are flip phones that delicious?

00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:36.410
Oh!

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:39.200
What's your favorite confection?

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:41.000
Uh... Kamome or Tamago!

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:44.420
-What about you, Hitomin?
-Hagi or Tsuki!

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:46.040
Yes!

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:52.510
One, two, three.

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:55.640
You've done excellent work.

00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:59.560
I look forward to working with you again.

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:01.890
Excuse me! Who are you?

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:06.560
Whatever.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:13.280
I've been tricked!

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:16.820
I will now present
the Sotoori Strategy findings.

00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:20.580
The probability of romance
developing for these women is...

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:22.370
exceedingly low.

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:23.370
Huh?

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:25.830
Gosh, this is so boring!

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:31.050
I wish they wouldn't work so hard
and recognize their own positions.

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:35.010
In their position, working is exactly
what they should be doing.

00:21:35.220 --> 00:21:36.890
How can you say that?

00:21:36.970 --> 00:21:39.550
They may be Self-Defense Force members,
but they are women first!

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:41.560
Love is a woman's work!

00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:45.020
Thank you, Sergeant Akishima.

00:21:45.100 --> 00:21:47.310
If something happens, we'll call you.

00:21:47.650 --> 00:21:51.270
Yes, sir. Though, I'm the one
expecting something to happen.

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:55.820
What about Technical Sergeant Amakasu?

00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:58.700
Yes. We are now friends.

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:00.620
Friends?

00:22:02.490 --> 00:22:03.580
Love...

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:08.250
No matter how much we avoid it,
it always comes unpredictably.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:11.920
To stop the law of love
from shaking the law of the land,

00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:16.260
they must devote
themselves wholly to the OTF.

00:22:17.050 --> 00:22:18.640
Driver, stop the car!

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:19.800
No...

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:22.010
just keep going.

00:22:31.610 --> 00:22:35.610
She has grown older... but still...

00:22:36.280 --> 00:22:38.950
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:11.670
Slowly, slowly.

00:24:11.750 --> 00:24:12.750
Amakasu!

00:24:12.870 --> 00:24:13.790
So fast!

00:24:13.960 --> 00:24:16.210
I wonder if they're impatient?

00:24:16.290 --> 00:24:18.800
My body's just reacting on its own.

00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:22.430
How much are you stuffing in
after a single date?
